<title>INDIA: India HPCL 1996/97 sales up 21.7 pct.</title>
<headline>India HPCL 1996/97 sales up 21.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian state-run refiner Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Ltd (HPCL) said on Thursday that its sales turnover had risen 21.7 percent to 180.89 bilion rupees during financial 1996/97 (April-March).</p>
<p>HPCL's turnover last year was 148.62 billion, a company spokeswoman said. Other details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
